---
// src/pages/ip-transit.astro  -  Flagship Reference Service Page
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Carrier-Neutral IP Transit Sourcing (10G-400G) | InfraHub"
  description="Compare Tier-1 and regional IP Transit providers. Evaluate 95th percentile burst billing, committed data rates, BGP community feeds, and cross-connect costs."
  canonicalPath="/ip-transit"
>
  <div class="service-page-wrapper">
    <div class="container service-container">
      
      <!-- Service Hero (Left-aligned, authoritative editorial) -->
      <header class="service-hero-band">
        <span class="service-kicker">NETWORK & CONNECTIVITY // PARTNER DELIVERED</span>
        <h1 class="service-title">Enterprise & Wholesale IP Transit</h1>
        <p class="service-lead">
          Connect your Autonomous System (ASN) to global Tier-1 backbones and regional transit providers. We evaluate port commitments, 95th percentile burst ratios, BGP community controls, and cross-connect fees across major colocation meet-me rooms.
        </p>
        <div class="service-hero-actions">
          <a href="/lets-talk?service=ip-transit" class="btn btn-accent btn-lg">Request Transit Comparison</a>
          <a href="#decision-framework" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg">Review Decision Factors</a>
        </div>
      </header>

      <!-- Problem Statement (Architectural Broadsheet Layout, no floating rounded cards) -->
      <section class="service-section">
        <span class="section-kicker">THE REQUIREMENT</span>
        <h2 class="section-headline">What problem are you trying to solve?</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">
          Selecting IP transit solely on price-per-megabit frequently leads to operational surprises: unexpected burst penalties, poor latency to specific regional eyeballs, or asymmetric routing loops. Technical buyers generally need transit to address three specific network realities:
        </p>
        
        <div class="architectural-triad">
          <div class="triad-item">
            <span class="triad-num">01</span>
            <h3 class="triad-title">Eyeball Reachability</h3>
            <p class="triad-desc">Direct, low-latency paths to consumer ISPs without traversing congested third-party peering fabrics or secondary settlement-free hops.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="triad-item">
            <span class="triad-num">02</span>
            <h3 class="triad-title">BGP Traffic Engineering</h3>
            <p class="triad-desc">Granular BGP community support to deprioritize backup upstreams, trigger blackholing (RTBH), or shape outbound flows by geographic destination.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="triad-item">
            <span class="triad-num">03</span>
            <h3 class="triad-title">Cost Predictability</h3>
            <p class="triad-desc">Balancing committed data rates (CDR) against unpredictable traffic spikes using verified 95th percentile burst calculations and port sizing.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Experience Note Module (Directive §18) -->
      <div class="experience-note">
        <span class="experience-note-kicker">INFRAHUB FIELD NOTE // WHAT BUYERS OFTEN MISS</span>
        <h3 class="experience-note-title">A low price per Mbps can cost more after cross-connects and bursts.</h3>
        <p class="experience-note-body">
          Carriers frequently quote attractive headline rates (€0.20-€0.45/Mbps) on 10G or 100G ports, but recover margin through mandatory datacenter cross-connect recurring fees, punitive 95th percentile burst tiers, or restrictive BGP traffic engineering communities. Before committing to an upstream provider, calculate the blended monthly cost including MMR patching and regional eyeball path quality.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Available Approaches -->
      <section class="service-section">
        <span class="section-kicker">ARCHITECTURE</span>
        <h2 class="section-headline">Available Transit Approaches</h2>
        <div class="approaches-list">
          <div class="approach-row">
            <div class="approach-col-title">
              <h3>Single Tier-1 Backbone</h3>
              <span class="approach-sub">Settlement-Free Global Core</span>
            </div>
            <div class="approach-col-desc">
              <p>Connect directly to a global Tier-1 network with extensive settlement-free peering across five continents.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="approach-col-points">
              <ul>
                <li>Lowest hop count for international enterprise destinations</li>
                <li>Strict SLA commitments on packet delivery and latency</li>
                <li>Higher cost per megabit; higher baseline commit requirements</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="approach-row">
            <div class="approach-col-title">
              <h3>Multi-Homed Blended Transit</h3>
              <span class="approach-sub">Managed BGP Blend</span>
            </div>
            <div class="approach-col-desc">
              <p>Purchase a pre-blended BGP transit mix delivered over a single cross-connect in your colocation facility.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="approach-col-points">
              <ul>
                <li>Automatic BGP best-path failover without running your own edge routers</li>
                <li>Economical commit thresholds for growing networks and platforms</li>
                <li>Less granular control over individual upstream carrier communities</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="approach-row">
            <div class="approach-col-title">
              <h3>Direct Dual Multi-Homing</h3>
              <span class="approach-sub">Independent Autonomous System</span>
            </div>
            <div class="approach-col-desc">
              <p>Contract two distinct Tier-1 / Tier-2 carriers terminated directly on your own redundant BGP border routers.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="approach-col-points">
              <ul>
                <li>Maximum fault tolerance against carrier-wide fiber cuts or BGP route leaks</li>
                <li>Full control over local preference, AS-path prepending, and FlowSpec</li>
                <li>Requires ASN ownership and dual MMR cross-connect recurring fees</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Technical Decision Factors Table -->
      <section class="service-section" id="decision-framework">
        <span class="section-kicker">TECHNICAL EVALUATION</span>
        <h2 class="section-headline">Decision Factors & Specifications</h2>
        <div class="factors-table-wrap">
          <table class="factors-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Evaluation Parameter</th>
                <th>Standard Configuration</th>
                <th>Why It Matters to the Buyer</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Port vs Commit (CDR)</strong></td>
                <td><span class="mono-text">100G port with 20G CDR</span></td>
                <td>Provides headroom to absorb DDoS spikes or viral traffic surges without port saturation.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>95th Percentile Billing</strong></td>
                <td><span class="mono-text">Top 5% burst samples discarded</span></td>
                <td>Protects against transient traffic spikes driving up monthly bandwidth commitments.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Route Feeds</strong></td>
                <td><span class="mono-text">Full Table (~950k v4 / ~200k v6)</span></td>
                <td>Enables precise BGP path selection; requires enterprise router memory (16GB+ RAM).</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>BGP Communities</strong></td>
                <td><span class="mono-text">Blackhole (RTBH), prepending</span></td>
                <td>Essential for autonomous DDoS defense and traffic steering during maintenance.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>MMR Cross-Connect Costs</strong></td>
                <td><span class="mono-text">Facility Monthly Recurring Charge</span></td>
                <td>Often costs more than the bandwidth itself in premium carrier-neutral datacenters.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- When It Fits vs When Another Approach Fits -->
      <section class="service-section">
        <div class="fit-editorial-split">
          <div class="fit-col">
            <h3 class="fit-title">When Direct IP Transit Fits</h3>
            <ul class="fit-list">
              <li>You own an Autonomous System Number (ASN) and portable IPv4/IPv6 allocations.</li>
              <li>You operate hardware in a carrier-neutral colocation facility.</li>
              <li>You require upstream path diversity, BGP multi-homing, and strict SLA latency bounds.</li>
              <li>You consume 1 Gbps or more of consistent outbound or inbound traffic.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="fit-col fit-alt">
            <h3 class="fit-title">When Another Approach Fits Better</h3>
            <ul class="fit-list">
              <li><strong>Dedicated Server / Cloud:</strong> Under 500 Mbps, host-bundled transit is significantly more economical.</li>
              <li><strong>Internet Exchange (IXP):</strong> If over 60% of traffic flows to local ISPs, an IXP port reduces transit spend.</li>
              <li><strong>Edge CDN:</strong> For static media delivery, an edge caching layer suppresses origin transit by 80%+.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- How InfraHub Helps (Architectural Dark Band, no cards inside cards) -->
      <section class="role-architectural-band">
        <div class="role-header">
          <span class="role-kicker">INFRAHUB SOURCING ROLE</span>
          <h2 class="role-headline">How InfraHub Helps You Evaluate IP Transit</h2>
          <p class="role-subhead">
            Rather than managing multiple carrier sales desks, InfraHub audits your facility meet-me room presence and provides independent technical benchmarking:
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="role-columns-grid">
          <div class="role-col-item">
            <span class="role-step-num">01</span>
            <h3 class="role-item-title">MMR On-Net Verification</h3>
            <p class="role-item-desc">We confirm which carriers have lit fiber in your exact datacenter meet-me room to avoid third-party local loop charges.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="role-col-item">
            <span class="role-step-num">02</span>
            <h3 class="role-item-title">Commit & Burst Benchmarking</h3>
            <p class="role-item-desc">We benchmark commercial rates for 10G, 40G, 100G, and 400G ports against current wholesale market intelligence.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="role-col-item">
            <span class="role-step-num">03</span>
            <h3 class="role-item-title">Cross-Connect Coordination</h3>
            <p class="role-item-desc">We assist with Letters of Authorization (LOA/CFA) and ensure fiber patch parameters match carrier specifications.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Active Offer (Clean, minimal, no AI banner styling) -->
      <section class="service-offer-card">
        <div class="offer-info">
          <span class="offer-kicker">CONFIRMED COMMERCIAL OPPORTUNITY</span>
          <h3 class="offer-title">100G IP Transit  -  Frankfurt</h3>
          <p class="offer-desc">20G Committed Data Rate on 100G port, burstable 95th percentile, from €1,450/month across Equinix and Interxion facilities.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/offers/100g-transit-frankfurt" class="btn btn-primary">
          <span>View Offer Details</span>
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true">
            <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line>
            <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19"></polyline>
          </svg>
        </a>
      </section>

      <!-- Footer CTA -->
      <div class="service-footer-cta">
        <h2 class="cta-headline">Discuss Your Transit Requirements</h2>
        <p class="cta-desc">Talk with an infrastructure sourcing advisor to evaluate carrier paths and commitments in your target facility.</p>
        <div class="cta-actions">
          <a href="/lets-talk?service=ip-transit" class="btn btn-accent btn-lg">Request Transit Sourcing</a>
          <a href="/how-we-work" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg">How We Work</a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .service-page-wrapper {
    background-color: #ffffff;
    padding: 64px 0 96px;
  }
  .service-container {
    max-width: 1080px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 72px;
  }

  /* Left-aligned, Authoritative Service Hero */
  .service-hero-band {
    max-width: 840px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
  }
  .service-kicker {
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .service-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 4.5vw, 3.4rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  .service-lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .service-hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }

  /* Section Anatomy */
  .service-section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .section-kicker {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .section-headline {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.3rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  .section-lead {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 820px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  /* Architectural Triad (Broadsheet Divider Layout) */
  .architectural-triad {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 32px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .architectural-triad {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: 36px;
    }
  }
  .triad-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }
  .triad-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
  }
  .triad-title {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  .triad-desc {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  /* Approaches List */
  .approaches-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .approach-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 28px 32px;
    background-color: #ffffff;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
  }
  .approach-row:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .approach-row {
      grid-template-columns: 240px 1.1fr 1.2fr;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 32px;
    }
  }
  .approach-col-title {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .approach-col-title h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  .approach-sub {
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .approach-col-desc p {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .approach-col-points ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 18px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  /* Table */
  .factors-table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }
  .factors-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    text-align: left;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .factors-table th, .factors-table td {
    padding: 16px 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
  }
  .factors-table th {
    background-color: var(--bg-secondary);
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .factors-table tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  .mono-text {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  /* When It Fits Split */
  .fit-editorial-split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 32px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .fit-editorial-split {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 40px;
    }
  }
  .fit-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 28px;
    background-color: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }
  .fit-title {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  .fit-list {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  /* Architectural Dark Band for InfraHub Role */
  .role-architectural-band {
    background-color: #0b1120;
    color: #ffffff;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 48px 40px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 40px;
  }
  .role-header {
    max-width: 720px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .role-kicker {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent-teal);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .role-headline {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.4rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: #ffffff;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }
  .role-subhead {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    color: #94a3b8;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .role-columns-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 28px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .role-columns-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: 32px;
    }
  }
  .role-col-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    padding-top: 18px;
  }
  .role-step-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent-teal);
  }
  .role-item-title {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #ffffff;
  }
  .role-item-desc {
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    color: #94a3b8;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* Clean Offer Card */
  .service-offer-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: 32px 36px;
    background-color: var(--bg-secondary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .service-offer-card {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: center;
    }
  }
  .offer-info {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }
  .offer-kicker {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .offer-title {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  .offer-desc {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* Footer CTA */
  .service-footer-cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);
  }
  .cta-headline {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  .cta-desc {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    max-width: 640px;
  }
  .cta-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
</style>
